        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Decide <strong class="text-white">match or contrast</strong> first, then pick the shade. Grey suits grey and mixed concrete pavers, tan suits warm and sandstone tones, charcoal frames large modern slabs, and ivory is beautiful in full sun and demanding anywhere damp.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Then test properly — a square yard, installed exactly as you would the rest, assessed the next day in daylight. Cured polymeric sand cannot be recoloured, so that single afternoon of patience is the difference between a patio you are happy with and one you grind the joints out of.
          </p>
